  "name": "no-printed-vp",
  "description": "A DIAGNOSTIC, NOT A PROPOSAL (Dean, 2026-08-09). Every printed VP in the corner of a card is set to 0, so a card can only be worth building for what its text does. Abilities, costs and thresholds are untouched, and the Endgame cards still score through their gameEnd text because that text IS their ability. The question it answers: are the upper tiers being built for their power or only for their 2 and 3 printed VP? Read the play rates and the activation counts, not the scores - with a fifth of the scoring removed the winning score is not comparable to the reference by construction.",
